{
  "method": "Reconstruct historical asset-local calls as they would have appeared using only previously completed outcomes. Allow a new asset-local call only when at least 50% of the preceding 24 months' completed asset-local calls were correct; require 60 calls spanning 9 signal months and 10 symbols. Outcomes on the signal date are excluded. Replayed asset-local and adaptive comparators use the same eligible observations, but select different calls. Flat prices count as misses.",
  "limitations": [
    "This candidate follows repeated testing on the same years and is exploratory, not an untouched or prospective evaluation; intervals do not adjust for research selection.",
    "Calls overlap and share market shocks; the gate's hit rate is not a calibrated probability. The gate can be unavailable and can reduce coverage dramatically.",
    "Present-day selected listings omit many delisted assets. Yahoo crypto differs from Binance. Costs, dividends, slippage and executable same-close entry are not modeled. No app labels change."
  ],
